    "done_when": "Measure only; no tracked file changes. Both halves of this measure run at one pinned revision, 76ed64992e8bdb54d7d01a7613ac120ef73a4f88, so together they are one full-suite run. Measure in a real git checkout, because tests read the repository's history, tags and HEAD: in your own worktree, if git rev-parse HEAD is not the pin, run git checkout --detach at the pin, then confirm git rev-parse HEAD equals it and git status --porcelain shows no tracked change. Run everything with the cwd in the worktree and PYTHONPATH pinned to it. (1) List its test files with ls tests/test_*.py sorted and keep the even-numbered files by position (counting from 1), written to the run directory as half-2.txt. Run them in ONE foreground call: timeout 2300 /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -n 8 -p no:cacheprovider -q --basetemp=$TMPDIR/pin-bt-2 followed by those files, redirected to the run directory as suite-half-2.log 2>&1, then append an EXIT line with its status. No command is backgrounded, no & and no nohup; stay in the turn until its EXIT line exists and never write status waiting for it. Record before and after it the 1-minute load average and squeue -u $USER -h -o '%i %j %M %R'; attribute any new job by WorkDir from scontrol show job and cancel nothing. Record wall time, the pass, fail, error and skip counts, and the count of lines naming PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning or 'Exception in thread'. (2) Re-run each failing or erroring id solo in the worktree, one id per foreground call, each with its own basetemp and log solo-1.log, solo-2.log and so on, each ending in an EXIT line; classify it deterministic (fails solo) or load-only (passes solo), and quote its first error line. (3) Attribute each deterministic id to a commit by git log -S on the asserted name or the pinned file, or unknown. suite-pin-half-2.md and suite-pin-half-2.json ({revision, files, wall_seconds, counts, thread_exception_lines, load_before, load_after, failing: [{id, first_error, class, attribution}]}) are written to the run directory and copied to /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/. The basetemp is deleted in a separate call after both reports exist.",
